package Striver_A2Z_Sheet.Sliding_Window_and_Two_Pointer;

/*
Logic:

We maintain a sliding window using two pointers (i and j).

1. Expand the window by moving j.
2. Count the number of zeros inside the current window.
3. As long as the number of zeros is less than k,
   include the current zero in the window.
4. When another zero is found and we have already used
   all k flips, the current window is a valid answer.
5. Store its length, then shrink the window from the left
   until one zero is removed.
6. Now there is room for the new zero, so include it
   and continue expanding.
7. After the loop, compare the last valid window with
   the maximum answer.

Time Complexity : O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
*/

